@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@feedVersionId = 1

# Replace these after calling GET /api/v1/routes.
@routeId = 100
@tripId = 1

### 1. Confirm that the NTA live feed is reachable.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/nta/realtime/summary

### 2. Preview real NTA stop-level delay updates.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/nta/realtime/trip-updates/preview?limit=5

### 3. Publish up to three valid NTA updates through Kafka.
# This is safe to rerun because identical feed snapshots use deterministic event IDs.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/nta/realtime/trip-updates/publish?feedVersionId={{feedVersionId}}&limit=3

### 4. Read the dashboard summary for the last 24 hours.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dashboard/summary?feedVersionId={{feedVersionId}}&hours=24

### 5. List routes and select a valid internal route ID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/routes

### 6. Get reliability for one route.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/routes/{{routeId}}/reliability

### 7. Find the least reliable routes in the last seven days.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/routes/reliability/worst?feedVersionId={{feedVersionId}}&hours=168&limit=10

### 8. Get the latest delay observations for one internal trip ID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/trips/{{tripId}}/delays?limit=10

### 9. Get reliability for one internal trip ID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/trips/{{tripId}}/reliability